{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795543749,"nonce":"BQzD+/2en3oAqphkVFbpQrL9XTo=","target":"eb418102af07a6eb43fec80b603433b438143c91e1aaa4d65aead1f9270dcce0","message":"`jno.core([p1, p2, conditions]).solve(coupling=...)` originally iterated eagerly. The fdm and fem participants took their interface data as stored values, so no gradient reached a parameter of a participant through the coupled fixed point. The plan was `lax.custom_root` on each window fixed point, as `jno.dd` does, with every participant taking its data as traced inputs.\n\n**Status on main.** This is done, in commits of #345 after the issue was filed. Commit 40ce7788 made every participant take its interface data and trainable parameters as traced inputs, and b764dda5 made the interface data values the iteration passes along instead of state on the data fields. Commit 06f4d4e9 added the implicit derivative: `Coupling._fixed_point` in `jno/_coupling/driver.py` runs the sweeps in a `lax.while_loop` and wraps them in `jax.lax.custom_root`, whose tangent is one GMRES solve inside a `custom_linear_solve`, so reverse mode solves the transposed system. Windows chain through their states, so a gradient crosses them. Commit 412a6621 makes `core.solve(coupling=...)` return trace nodes (`FunctionCall`) when a participant has a trainable parameter, so a `jno.core` loss trains it. Commit e535cb18 extends this to three kinds of participant in series (fem flux read-back, fdm flux sample).\n\n**Fix and guards.** `tests/test_coupling_gradients.py` checks a steady coupling against the closed form of two slabs in series (dT_i/dk_a = -k_b / (k_a + k_b)^2, to rtol 1e-8), a transient contact against a central difference (rtol 1e-6), three kinds in series, and `jno.core` training a conductivity through a coupling. `tests/test_coupling_participants.py` covers a participant under `jit` with a gradient by its data and a parameter.\n\n**What is still missing.** The compiled or differentiated fixed point relaxes with Aitken or a fixed factor only; `accel=\"iqn-ils\"` raises `NotImplementedError` there (#366). `docs/coupling.md` lists this under Limitations.","files":null}]}